  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Investing for impact against Tuberculosis - Nigeria (01-Jan-2019-31-Dec-2020)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Nigeria, Tuberculosis, Institute of Human Virology Nigeria (IHVN)This program has the following goals: To ensure universal access to high-quality, patient-centred, prevention, diagnosis and treatment services for TB, TB/HIV and DR-TB by 2020..  Responsive and resilient health systems that promote universal access to quality health care services by 2020. The objectives of this program are: To increase case notification rate of all forms of TB from 55.1/100,000 population in 2017 to 287 per 100,000 population in 2020.  To increase TB treatment success rate from 85% in 2017 to 90% in 2020 among drug susceptible patients.  To enrol 100% of diagnosed DR-TB patients on appropriate treatment by 2020.  Strengthen health systems for delivery of packages of essential health care services</narrative>
  </description>
